---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Use · My Family Allowance">
  <Fragment slot="nav">
    <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" href="/">Home</a>
  </Fragment>

  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: August 31, 2026</p>

    <p>
      By using My Family Allowance, you agree to these terms. If you do not
      agree, please do not use the app.
    </p>

    <h2>What the service is</h2>
    <p>
      My Family Allowance helps parents track kids’ allowance balances, memos,
      and weekly credits. It is a personal tracking tool, not a bank, payment
      processor, or financial advisor.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>
      You sign in with Google. You are responsible for activity under your
      account and for keeping your Google account secure. Do not share your
      parent login with people who should not manage your family’s data.
    </p>

    <h2>Family page access</h2>
    <p>
      Each family gets a short private URL and a shared password. Anyone with
      that URL and password can view kid balances and transaction history. You
      are responsible for who you share those with.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Use the app for your own family’s allowance tracking. Do not try to break
      into other families’ data, abuse the service, or use it for anything
      illegal.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy and availability</h2>
    <p>
      Balances and history reflect what you enter and what the weekly job
      credits. The service may be unavailable at times for maintenance, outages,
      or other reasons. There is no guarantee of uninterrupted access.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The app is provided as is, without warranties of any kind. Use it at your
      own risk. It is not a substitute for your own records or professional
      financial advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent allowed by law, the operator is not liable for lost
      data, incorrect balances, downtime, or any damages that come from using or
      being unable to use the service.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may change over time. Continued use after an update means you
      accept the revised terms. The date at the top of this page will be updated
      when changes are posted.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms can go to the site operator via the contact
      link on the home page footer.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
